  "director_notes": "Directed from a game-capture reference whose jet was a flat, blown-out white bar and whose splash read yellow-green over grass. Fixes: (1) the jet is mid-blue with only a thin white thread, so it reads as water on any background; (2) a 320 ms gather and a 180 ms visible travel replace the reference's instant on/off, so the hit has a cause; (3) the splash is a fountain that keeps spraying for the whole contact and falls back with gravity, plus mist, ripples and a puddle, so water has weight and leaves a mark. The reference's camera cuts are not copied: this is one continuous shot. Decals: a wide dark wet patch, a brighter puddle that spreads out (grow_ms) and splash droplets around it, all alpha-blended. The puddle and wet patch outlive the spell. Look pass: the jet is a churning water column (beam style water: noise-eaten ragged edges, foam streaks and bright rims flowing to the target, surges that swell and pinch it, droplets peeling off), the splash is liquid droplets (sparks look droplet) with a tall crown and a white foam burst, and wet decals stay behind."
